  "summary": "Messages queue cleared under RBC-RX-05: 7 items closed (6 original plus 1 that came in while I worked). Three results arrived partway through and reversed or changed two decisions; I corrected all of them (§7).\n\npt-0027 Frank Odum (lisinopril 10 mg): First renewed for 90 days + 1 refill. The August outside potassium of 5.9 came from a hemolyzed sample, so it didn't count; the valid K was 4.5 (Jan 2026). I also ordered a repeat BMP (sr-t0002). Then an outside BMP collected 10/20 arrived: K 5.8 on an acceptable sample. That stops the refill, so I cancelled the renewal (mr-t0001). Urgent task to Dr. Okafor (task-t0019, focus mr-00283). The patient got a corrected message: don't restart lisinopril until contacted, with emergency warning signs. Repeat BMP sr-t0002 is still active for you to decide on.\n\npt-0030 Samuel Price (lisinopril 20 mg; metformin 1000 mg twice daily, asked for 4 times): The metformin requests were handled as one request: renewed for 90 days + 1 refill (mr-t0006), based on eGFR 58 and the outside HbA1c of 7.1% from 8/19. Lisinopril was first renewed (mr-t0005). Then the lab corrected the 10/6 creatinine from 1.36 to 1.49. That is 35.5% above the 1.10 measured before the dose increase, within 4 weeks of it, which counts the same as K ≥5.5. I cancelled mr-t0005. Urgent task to Dr. Okafor (task-t0020, focus mr-00295). Corrected message sent to the patient; metformin is unchanged.\n\npt-0031 Marcus Webb (lisinopril 10 mg, metformin 500 mg): Metformin renewed for 90 days + 1 refill (mr-t0013). The 10/14 eGFR of 39 is marked entered-in-error (wrong patient's sample), so the valid eGFR is 92 and HbA1c 6.9%. Lisinopril first got 30 days with no refills plus a BMP order, because no BMP was on file within 12 months. A valid BMP from 10/22 then arrived (K 4.6), so I replaced it with a 90-day supply + 1 refill (mr-t0021). The BMP order sr-t0012 is no longer needed, but I can't cancel lab orders, so I left a routine task asking you to cancel it (task-t0026). Updated message sent to the patient.\n\nEach patient got a reply, and each chart has a note recording the reasons. Three results-queue items that came with the new results (inbox-a0001, a0002, a0004) are still open for your review. I didn't touch the other results-queue items or other patients.",
